Package: pathwaydepth
Title: Depth Features for Spatial Pathway Graphs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", email = "bhadury@upenn.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-2966-0678")),
    person("Ashley P.", "Tsang", role = "aut"),
    person("Dipankar", "Ray", role = "ctb"),
    person("Kiran", "Lagisetty", role = "ctb"),
    person("Arvind", "Rao", role = "aut"))
Description: Converts the edge weights of a small weighted graph into
    edge-level depth features under two reference frames: the distribution of
    the same edge across a reference cohort (population-referenced depth) and
    the distribution of all edges within the same graph (within-sample depth).
    The depth is the univariate halfspace (Tukey) depth scaled to the unit
    interval, stabilised by subsampling the reference set. The package also
    provides the graph completion step, patient-level data splitting, a
    random forest classifier tuned on out-of-bag predictions, and the
    evaluation tools used to compare lung adenocarcinoma with lung squamous
    cell carcinoma on spatial pathway graphs derived from The Cancer Genome
    Atlas histology slides. The lung graphs are not included, because the
    licence of the data they are derived from does not allow derivatives to
    be distributed; simulated graphs are provided for examples.
